# =============================================================================
# Build context for the images (Dockerfile).
# =============================================================================
# The `loader` stage is fully self-contained: it apt-installs pgloader + the psql
# client and inlines its load script via a Dockerfile heredoc. It COPYs NOTHING
# from the tree. The other stages need source:
#   * `go-build`/`reader` -> the Go VIEW-reader under file_analyzer/views/go (+ file_analyzer/views/sql).
#   * `engine`            -> the whole file_analyzer/ Python package (runs `python -m file_analyzer.main`).
#
# So: exclude everything, then re-include the file_analyzer/ package. This keeps the
# context to just what the source-using stages compile/run.
*

!file_analyzer/**

# Never bring caches or build outputs into the context.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
file_analyzer/views/go/repo-reader
file_analyzer/views/go/repo-reader.exe
file_analyzer/views/go/*.exe
file_analyzer/router/go/analysis-plane
file_analyzer/router/go/*.exe
file_analyzer/router/java/out/

# (The AnalysisEngine artifacts are NOT baked into any image -- they are
#  bind-mounted at runtime: /artifacts (loader/reader/engine) and /workspace
#  (engine source repo) by db.docker-compose.yml.)
